    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0568" n="546" xml:id="pg546"/>

                <head>No. 82.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Although by a literal construction of the Senate Article, cases of bad faith or
                    willful misconduct may be held to be within its scope, it is inconceivable that
                    such cases can ever be the subject of diplomatic correspondence with a view to
                    pecuniary compensation between two Powers such as those now concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
